    {
      "source_number": "903",
      "independent_solution": "Use t equal to the original variable squared, t>=0; reject negative t and restore both signs for positive t. a: (t-1)(t+2), roots +-1. b: (t-9)(t+1), roots +-3. c: (t-16)(t+9), roots +-4. d: (4t-1)(9t-1), roots +-1/2,+-1/3. e: (2t-1)(8t-1), roots +-sqrt(2)/2,+-sqrt(2)/4. f: (t+5)(t+10), no real roots. g: (t-4)^2, roots +-2, each repeated. h: (3t-1)^2, roots +-sqrt(3)/3, each repeated. i: t(t-25), roots {-5,0,5}. j: t(t+0.16), only root0. Zero is repeated in i/j but is listed once.",
      "coverage": {"verdict": "pass", "evidence": "q05 covers a/b, q06 c/f, q07 d/e, q08 g/h and q09 i/j. All ten formulas and complete real root sets are represented. Pairing contrasts negative-square rejection, two positive branches, repeated roots and zero roots. Independent written factorization, branch rejection and multiplicity explanation are declared production losses."}
