      "independent_solution": "Intersect the x-axis by f(x)=0 and the y-axis by x=0. a: x-axis {(-3,0),(-1,0),(1,0),(3,0)}, y-axis {(0,9)}. b: x-axis {(-sqrt(3),0),(sqrt(3),0)}, y-axis {(0,-3)}. c: f(x)=(x^2+1)^2+5>=6, so no x-axis intersection; y-axis {(0,6)}. d: x^2(x^2+36)=0 only at x=0, and f(0)=0, so both axes meet the graph at the same single distinct point(0,0).",
